    "created_at": "2022-12-17T18:55:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-12-17T18:55:35Z",
    "body": "> @jakearchibald @youennf @rayankans does any of you think this boolean is worth having for CORS? I think I'd rather allow whitespace in CORS for the `Range` header so we can keep `Range` header parsing consistent. In particular this would allow an arbitrary number of 0x09 and 0x20 after `bytes=`. I don't see the security benefit.\r\n> \r\n> (We also use this parser for `blob:` URL requests and there we already allow whitespace.)\r\n\r\nI've tested Blink and WebKit and both disallow the whitespace allowed in HTTP-RANGE as tested [here](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/37569). Would it make sense to remove the boolean, but add a note that some implementations don't allow this optional whitespace?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
